043731204141001-ce180279-8b2d-4655-9045-c71fa16e0a83"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"24744fbc903ea43e00ba34598132e52860eb3f5175cc999660ab3b8255060494","event_uuid":"f4814ab8-c592-4ee9-b398-59b0d6d2b423","position":{"commit_sha":"885c57a7053d802e785a4ad2e0481745a42b8ae2","position":"1787043733427504001-f4814ab8-c592-4ee9-b398-59b0d6d2b423"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Confirmed RCA before Phase 2\n\nMechanism: `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py:149-166` copies the full ordered `os.environ` into the returned `box` fixture. Pytest default/long traceback formatting renders function arguments through a 240-character `saferepr`; therefore ambient credentials early enough in that mapping are emitted verbatim in the ordinary failure header.\n\nDiscriminating proof used a fully sanitized `env -i`: with a synthetic sentinel inserted before PATH, the real existing failing node under default `pytest -q` printed the sentinel inside `box = {env: ...}`. Moving it after PATH hid it by repr truncation, explaining the first false-negative probe. Running the same failure with `--tb=short` removed the sentinel while child stdout/stderr and the assertion stayed unchanged, rejecting subprocess/autodeploy logging as the carrier. No real secret was logged.\n\nLegitimacy: defect. The ticket AC requires a synthetic secret to be absent from failure output, and the security rubric forbids plaintext secrets in logs. A prior closed sibling `spodumene-stoned-arkshell` records the same broad-environment repr exposure.\n\nCaller gate: only `_run` consumes `box[env]`; the harness needs PATH plus explicit test-owned variables (`DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX`, `HEALTH_TIMEOUT`). Sanitized reproductions prove it does not depend on ambient credentials.\n\nConstruct sweep found seven semantically equivalent returned-fixture mappings: test_autodeploy_materialize_probe.py, test_autodeploy_fetch_secrets.py, test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py, test_autodeploy_health_gate.py, test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py, test_observability_exit.py, and tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli.py. Each requires same-scope repair or a linked follow-up under Step 7.","timestamp":1787022128995194001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Repair verification report\n\nProblem: pytest failure rendering could print arbitrary ambient credentials returned inside the autodeploy review-drain fixture.\n\nProven root cause/proof: the fixture copied ordered os.environ; default long traceback renders fixture args through 240-char saferepr. Sanitized sentinel-before-PATH runs leaked; --tb=short did not, proving pytest funcarg rendering was the carrier.\n\nTest: held-out real nested-pytest oracle tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py was RED before repair. Its final trigger uses a fake bash on required PATH so the target fails independently of the environment-removal fix. It is GREEN after repair. Restoring dict(os.environ) returned it to RED; the scoped fix was restored.\n\nFix: tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py now passes only stubbed PATH plus explicit harness variables; DEPLOY_DEFER_MAX/HEALTH_TIMEOUT remain mutable by tests. No dependency, production behavior, or existing assertion changed.\n\nSafety/gates: review-drain plus oracle 15 passed; make lint and make typecheck passed. No ambient credential was used or logged.\n\nSiblings: seven confirmed same-class fixtures were inventoried. Child bug dumbstruck-wonderful-xiphosuran (3402-7143-2e14-4d1a) tracks their parametrized RED-to-GREEN repair; hierarchy already expresses discovery, so rebar correctly rejected a redundant discovered_from link. Parity channels outside pytest fixtures are N/A.\n\nReplication: ordinary default traceback still renders the box fixture on the seeded failure, but its env contains no synthetic sentinel or other arbitrary ambient values.","timestamp":1787022567330024001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI RCA for Change 1847 PS1 (run 32098530041): deterministic test-failure, not infrastructure. All Python 3.11/3.12/3.13 shards failed the repo-root isolation guard on the same newly-created `.pytest_cache`, attributed to different concurrent tests only because xdist observed the shared leak asynchronously. The patchset adds `test_failure_rendering_does_not_expose_ambient_environment`, whose nested `python -m pytest` runs with `cwd=_REPO` and does not pass `-p no:cacheprovider`; unlike the outer CI suite, the child therefore enables pytest cache and creates `_REPO/.pytest_cache` mid-run. Local discriminating reproduction on the patchset: with `.pytest_cache` absent, `pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n 4 tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py` returns one passed + one teardown error naming exactly `[`.pytest_cache`]`. This rules out the production fixture env narrowing and Python-version behavior; the defect is the new nested-test invocation failing to sandbox/disable its own cache. Fix must keep nested pytest artifacts outside REPO_ROOT (or disable cache) while preserving the environment-redaction oracle. No repush until the currently pending CI runs complete, per one-pending-run discipline.","timestamp":1787028553424263001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI repair evidence for Change 1847 PS2 preparation. Held-out oracle was the outer repo-isolation lifecycle with cache disabled and xdist enabled; on PS1 it deterministically failed because the nested security-test pytest created `.pytest_cache` in REPO_ROOT. Blind fixer did not see that oracle and changed only the nested child argv: `-p no:cacheprovider` disables its persistent cache, and `--basetemp <outer tmp_path>/nested-pytest` confines remaining runtime artifacts to test-owned storage. Held-out GREEN: 1 passed. Exact-defect mutation (remove those four argv entries) returned the same `.pytest_cache` repo-leak teardown ERROR; restoring the fix returned GREEN. Focused security + autodeploy suite: 13 passed. Ruff check/format and diff check pass. Scope/safety: test-only, no production/workflow/dependency change, no weakened assertion; child still reaches seeded PATH failure and sentinel remains absent. CI_RESULT for PS1: {\"run_id\":\"32098530041\",\"status\":\"failed\",\"failure_type\":\"test-failure\",\"failure_details\":\"all py3.11/3.12/3.13 shards detected nested pytest .pytest_cache leaking into REPO_ROOT\",\"fixes_applied\":[\"disabled nested cacheprovider\",\"redirected nested basetemp under tmp_path\"],\"retry_count\":0}. PS2 will be pushed after the still-pending CI runs finish, preserving one-pending-run discipline.","timestamp":1787028968997574001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator-attested evidence: RebarBotNava executed the sanitized nested-pytest RED probe before repair; with a synthetic first-position sentinel, default-long traceback rendered the sentinel, while --tb=short removed it without changing the seeded subprocess failure. No real credential was used or recorded. The final held-out oracle went GREEN and the exact dict(os.environ) mutation returned it to RED, as recorded in the repair report. Gerrit change 1847 merged as 034e17209c after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments; canonical successful CI artifact: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/32101886011.","timestamp":1787042237032473001}],"created_at":1786832134098619001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6890ce29-b2e6-4fd8-b89f-453230facb19","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c7e4-4df1-1477-4db1"},{"link_uuid":"d99ae53f-b0ef-42d1-82bf-c722a4275cda","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"846d-86e6-9c6d-42d4"},{"link_uuid":"291ad971-d91f-4c57-9569-7897de1c9010","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8fac-0876-f8a4-46fe"}],"description":"## Context\nBefore merged Change 1847, at the parent of commit 034e17209c, tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py constructed `env = dict(os.environ)` and returned that mapping inside the `box` fixture value. A deliberate nested-pytest RED probe against that pre-fix revision placed a synthetic sentinel before PATH and observed pytest default-long traceback rendering print it; no real credential value was used or recorded. Commit 034e17209c repaired that defect: the current file at lines 149-165 now constructs a narrow PATH-plus-harness allowlist. This ticket records and verifies the already-landed repair; it does not claim the current fixture still copies the full environment. The performance ticket must not absorb this unrelated security fix.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce on the pre-fix revision with a synthetic first-position sentinel in the ambient environment and a deliberate assertion failure.\n- Change the fixture boundary to pass only required environment variables while preserving the real bash subprocess environment needed by the tests.\n- Audit sibling subprocess fixtures for the same `dict(os.environ)`-inside-rendered-fixture shape.\n- Prove on the repaired revision that the synthetic sentinel never appears in pytest default-long failure output while the autodeploy suite remains behaviorally green.\n\n## Scope and alternative rationale\nThe construct sweep separates two runtime carriers rather than deferring equivalent leaks. This parent and child dumbstruck-wonderful-xiphosuran own the eight decorated fixtures whose returned values pytest renders as function arguments; explicit allowlists are correct there because minimal-parent runs prove their consumers need only declared harness values. The remaining broad mappings are test-local or helper values exposed only when subprocess startup itself raises. Some intentionally forward the invoking pytest environment or environment-only live-service credentials, so applying the fixture allowlist would break their contract. Follow-up antiutopic-toadyish-goldfinch owns all 103 of those sites as one atomic shared representation-safe mapping migration, with a repository guard and exact child-value preservation test. A repo-wide allowlist was rejected because it would drop required values; independent per-file wrappers were rejected because they would duplicate the same diagnostic boundary without enforcement. Pytest `--tb=short` was a useful negative control but was rejected as remediation because it globally reduces debugging detail and only masks this traceback carrier; the repaired fixture boundary remains safe under the default long traceback. ADR 0041 governs durable LLM diagnostic fields rather than pytest fixture representations; its fail-closed allowlist posture is nevertheless followed for these decorated fixtures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] [operator-attested] A deterministic regression test fails on the pre-fix revision because a synthetic ambient secret appears in captured pytest failure rendering.\n  provenance: environment=sanitized-red-probe-034e17209c; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=simulation — real nested pytest default-long traceback with first-position synthetic sentinel\n- [x] The synthetic secret is absent from failure output after the fix.\n- [x] Required PATH and autodeploy environment behavior remains covered through the real bash subprocess.\n- [x] Sibling occurrences are inventoried and either fixed or linked as follow-ups.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Repository gates and Gerrit votes pass before closure.\n  provenance: environment=gerrit-ci-run-32101886011; principal=rebar-ci-bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — canonical Gerrit Verified and LLM-Review gates for merged change 1847","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py","reason":"narrow the returned fixture environment to required values"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_env_repr_security.py","reason":"prove failure rendering cannot expose ambient values and sandbox nested pytest artifacts"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","846d-86e6-9c6d-42d4"],["relates_to","8fac-0876-f8a4-46fe"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ce180279-8b2d-4655-9045-c71fa16e0a83","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["security","tests"],"ticket_id":"fc43-3c50-ec6c-4a3e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Prevent autodeploy test failures from printing ambient credentials","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d351fe70-8183-4de5-a26b-2b9261d74e20","177dba69-4b19-45bd-bad8-5c4f4d3998e9","f6bcf772-1179-46e3-a4e1-d3f0d565e17f","16e3f35a-2cd4-4132-85fe-95066f162f67","0085d3b5-4c22-48ed-be68-8ae16039633f","d99ae53f-b0ef-42d1-82bf-c722a4275cda","95e2d0e3-f767-40ba-968b-1a28c78ae621","c894749e-80a0-4d01-a9d0-681a45b8c1dd","291ad971-d91f-4c57-9569-7897de1c9010","381ce2e8-3fa4-